- sidecar > A Rust binary named tracequest-sidecar lives in a sidecar/ directory at the project root and is built with Cargo @spec @implemented
- sidecar > The sidecar exposes a scan CLI: tracequest-sidecar scan --roots <json_array> --filter <optional_str> outputs a JSON array of session objects with path, project, file, size, mtime, source fields identical to JS findSessions @spec @implemented
- label: sidecar > The sidecar exposes an index CLI: tracequest-sidecar index --index-path <path> --version <int> with session input via --sessions-stdin (preferred) or --sessions-json <json_array>, outputting a JSON object keyed by session path whose values contain metadata fields; freshly parsed and search-stale entries also include transient termFreqs for Node SearchIndex insertion, and termFreqs is not part of returned JS buildIndex metadata
  id: mmq
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'runSidecar index passes sessions on stdin with --sessions-stdin|buildIndex sends searchStale stdin to sidecar, inserts termFreqs into SearchIndex, and drops searchText' test/sidecar-gate.test.js && cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_keeps_term_freqs_for_stdout_but_cache_omits_them
  tags: [spec, implemented, sidecar-index-output-facts]
- label: sidecar > The Node sessions.js module delegates findSessions/buildIndex to tracequest-sidecar only when the sidecar gate is open and a valid sidecar path is resolved; TRACEQUEST_NO_SIDECAR=1, missing/invalid binaries, spawn failures, non-zero exits, or parse failures fall back to the JS implementation
  id: 5dl
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'sidecar gate env|sidecar gate JS fallback paths|sidecar implicit skip|sidecar enabled path|runSidecar warn \+ JS fallback' test/sidecar-gate.test.js test/sessions/warn-sidecar.test.js
  tags: [spec, implemented, sidecar-gate-facts]
- label: sidecar > The Rust scan command walks all 6 agent data roots in parallel using rayon, returning session objects sorted by mtime descending
  command: grep -q '\.par_iter()' sidecar/src/scan.rs && cd sidecar && cargo test test_scan_sorts_results_by_mtime_desc
  tags: [spec, implemented, sidecar-architecture-facts]
- label: sidecar > The Rust sidecar uses memory-mapped file I/O (memmap2) for session files larger than 512KB to avoid loading entire files into heap memory
  command: grep -q 'size > 512 \* 1024' sidecar/src/indexer.rs && cd sidecar && cargo test test_index_claude_large_file_exceeds_mmap_threshold
  tags: [spec, implemented, sidecar-architecture-facts]
- label: sidecar > The Rust sidecar normalizes tool names using the same canonical mapping as JS normalizeToolName
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_normalize_tool_name
  tags: [spec, implemented, sidecar-architecture-facts]
- id: 32t
  label: sidecar > The Rust sidecar handles all 7 source formats: claude, codex, cursor, cursor-cloud, factory, grok, and opencode
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_infer_source && cargo test structure && cargo test basic
  tags: [spec, implemented, sidecar-architecture-facts, cursor-cloud]
- label: sidecar > The Rust index command fails closed on a session whose source is not one of the seven known sources (claude, codex, cursor, cursor-cloud, factory, grok, opencode): there is no catch-all fallback to index_claude, build_index returns an error for the whole batch, the process writes an explicit error naming the source and session path to stderr and exits non-zero, and neither stdout nor index.json ever receives an entry for that session — including when a previously persisted entry for it is mtime-matched in the cache
  id: z9k
  command: ! grep -q '_ => index_claude' sidecar/src/indexer.rs && cd sidecar && cargo test --test index_unknown_source && cargo test test_build_index_errors_on_unknown_source
  tags: [spec, sidecar-fail-closed-facts, implemented, cursor-cloud]

## search
- label: sidecar > The Rust index command computes tokenizer-equivalent per-session term-frequency maps (termFreqs) for freshly parsed and search-stale sessions, so SearchIndex Postings are identical regardless of whether JS or Rust parsed the session
  id: fzs
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'search-relevant index fields match for every discovered session|shared needle: eight hits with identical paths, seven sources, and snippets' test/sidecar-index-search-parity.test.js
  tags: [search, implemented, search-tokenizer-contract, cursor-cloud]
- label: sidecar > Rust and JS tokenizer equivalence is verified by a shared fixture: both sides produce the same term-frequency map for the same corpus fixture file
  id: ovv
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'JS/Rust parity: accumulateTermFreqs over corpus fixture matches Rust termfreqs.json' test/sessions/search-tokenizer.test.js && cd sidecar && cargo test test_tokenize_corpus_fixture
  tags: [spec, search, implemented, search-tokenizer-contract]
- label: sidecar > The Rust index command stdout includes termFreqs and no searchText for freshly parsed and search-stale entries; termFreqs is a transient term-frequency map for SearchIndex insertion, not persisted full-text content
  id: c7m
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_keeps_term_freqs_for_stdout_but_cache_omits_them && cargo test test_build_index_reparses_search_stale_cache_hit_for_term_freqs
  tags: [search, implemented, sidecar-index-output-facts]
- label: sidecar > The Rust index command's index.json disk-cache write-back persists metadata-only entries: neither searchText nor termFreqs is written to index.json; when termFreqs is present it is emitted on stdout only and persisted solely in search.idx by Node
  id: 9ct
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'sidecar-emitted termFreqs are stripped from index.json and persisted in search.idx' test/index-writers.test.js && cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_keeps_term_freqs_for_stdout_but_cache_omits_them
  tags: [search, implemented, search-index-output-contract]
- label: sidecar > Node passes the set of sessions missing from the SearchIndex to the sidecar as additional stale sessions; the sidecar re-parses any session that is mtime-stale or search-stale and emits termFreqs for each, so mtime-matched cache reuse never starves the SearchIndex of term data
  id: 8rj
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'buildIndex sends searchStale stdin to sidecar, inserts termFreqs into SearchIndex, and drops searchText' test/sidecar-gate.test.js && cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_reparses_search_stale_cache_hit_for_term_freqs
  tags: [spec, search, implemented, search-index-output-contract]
- label: sidecar > The Node side merges sidecar-emitted termFreqs into the SearchIndex through the same incremental insert/remove path used by the JS indexers, so search.idx never depends on which pipeline ran
  id: wyt
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'sidecar-emitted termFreqs are stripped from index.json and persisted in search.idx|cached session postings survive when sidecar omits termFreqs for it|second sidecar pass leaves SI stable' test/index-writers.test.js
  tags: [search, implemented, search-index-output-contract]

# cursor
- id: sd3
  label: The Rust sidecar scan/index path handles all seven source formats: claude, codex, cursor, cursor-cloud, factory, grok, and opencode; Cursor scan discovers ~/.cursor/projects rows and Cursor index reuses Claude-family JSONL indexing
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_infer_source && cargo test test_scan_cursor_structure && cargo test test_index_cursor_reuses_claude_jsonl
  tags: [spec, cursor, sidecar, implemented, cursor-cloud]

# cursor-cloud
- label: KNOWN_SOURCES in sidecar/src/indexer.rs is a [&str; 7] array including "cursor-cloud", the Source enum in sidecar/src/types.rs gains a CursorCloud variant, and the fail-closed contract of fact z9k is unchanged for genuinely unknown sources (JS twin of fact ccsv in cursor-cloud.facts)
  id: ccr7
  command: grep -q '\[&str; 7\]' sidecar/src/indexer.rs && grep -q 'cursor-cloud' sidecar/src/indexer.rs && cd sidecar && cargo test test_infer_source
  tags: [spec, cursor-cloud, sidecar, implemented]
- label: sidecar scan infers Source::CursorCloud for a root whose path contains both "tracequest" and "cursor-cloud", and scan_cursor_cloud walks <root>/<project-slug>/<agentId>.jsonl emitting source "cursor-cloud" rows with project, size, and mtime, so sidecar scan output matches JS discovery for the same seven-root set (JS twin of fact ccdw)
  id: ccri
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_infer_source_cursor_cloud && cargo test test_scan_cursor_cloud_structure
  tags: [spec, cursor-cloud, sidecar, implemented]
- label: Rust index_cursor_cloud stays in parity with JS indexCursorCloudJsonl: it consumes the session_meta first line (model, createdAt/updatedAt yielding durationMs = max(0, updatedAt - createdAt), firstPrompt fallback to name), reuses Cursor's Claude-family row indexing and token estimation for the message rows, and falls back to the model literal "cursor-cloud" when meta.model is absent (JS twins: facts ccix and ccmf)
  id: ccrx
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_index_cursor_cloud_meta && cargo test test_index_cursor_cloud_reuses_cursor_rows
  tags: [spec, cursor-cloud, sidecar, implemented]
